Phase 8 items 1-2 (sandbox-gateway + cloud-worker, docs/24) — E2E proof
Date: 2026-09-12

Real processes over real TCP, THE canonical Core runtime in the cloud
worker (no second runtime):
1. Handshake over TCP generalized in the canonical protocol crate
   (handshake_stream/Connection::accept_stream/over_stream) — same
   Challenge/Hello/AuthResult HMAC proof scheme as the local socket
   transport. DEFECT CAUGHT BY THE E2E: the gateway initially ran the
   CLIENT side of the handshake on accepted connections (both sides
   waiting for a Challenge — deadlock); the samples caught it and the
   server side (accept_stream) is now the gateway path.
2. Gateway (tenant-bound substrate boundary): boot-secret auth, worker
   lease per TENANT, opaque framed relay (the gateway never parses the
   SurfaceProtocol payload).
3. Cloud worker: leases a tenant and serves guest envelopes through
   CoreServices::handle against the REAL durable event store — cloud
   tasks write the same canonical events as local (state asserted in
   the worker's store).
4. TENANT ISOLATION (docs/24 § Multi-tenancy): tenant-2 guest gets an
   explicit "no worker"; a tenant-2 guest FORGING the envelope tenant
   "tenant-1" is refused ("cross-tenant denied") — the REGISTRATION is
   the only trusted tenant source.
5. LOSS/RECOVERY: worker killed → guest gets an explicit typed failure
   (never a hang, never fabricated success); a re-attached worker serves
   the DURABLE state — the task created before the kill is in the
   recovered fleet.

Test evidence: cargo test -p modbit-sandbox-gateway --test gateway_e2e
(gateway_relays_real_core_work_and_enforces_tenant_isolation) — green;
full workspace 551 tests 0 failed.

